# Version Control Standards

When asked to generate a commit message or summarize changes, you MUST use the Conventional Commits format.

### 1. Format
`<type>(<optional scope>): <description>`

### 2. Allowed Types
* `feat`: A new feature (Frontend UI or Backend route).
* `fix`: A bug fix.
* `refactor`: A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature.
* `chore`: Updating build tasks, package manager configs, etc.
* `style`: Formatting, missing semi-colons, MUI style tweaks.

### 3. Constraints
* Keep the description line under 50 characters.
* Do not use uppercase letters at the start of the description.
* Do not end the description with a period.
* If a longer explanation is needed, add a blank line after the description and write a bulleted list of the exact technical changes.